what is wrong with my code? billboardLong<- billboard|> pivot_longer(cols = "wk"), names_to = "week", values_to = "rank"

here are two problems with your code:

Your code:
billboardLong <- billboard |> 
  pivot_longer(cols = "wk"), names_to = "week", values_to = "rank"


1. Your parentheses close too early.

You put ) after "wk", which ends pivot_longer() before names_to and values_to. Those arguments need to be inside the parentheses.

2. cols = "wk" selects the wrong column name.

The Billboard dataset has columns named wk1, wk2, etc. Use starts_with("wk") to select all of them.
Correct code
billboardLong <- billboard |>
  pivot_longer(
    cols = starts_with("wk"),
    names_to = "week",
    values_to = "rank"
  )
```
